import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="AWD system overview">
  <h1>AWD system overview</h1>
  <p>This page distinguishes the two AWD architectures available in the 2021 S60 range. The illustration below represents the mechanical AWD layout used on applicable T5 AWD and T6 AWD models. It is not a parts diagram, hydraulic schematic, wiring diagram, or service procedure. Exact component names and configuration must be confirmed against VIN-specific Volvo service information.</p>

  <figure class="diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="awd-title awd-desc">
      <title id="awd-title">Simplified all-wheel-drive power flow</title>
      <desc id="awd-desc">On mechanical AWD models, the engine and transmission drive the front axle, with a power take-off and propeller shaft carrying torque toward the rear drive unit and rear axle. T8 Recharge uses an electric rear axle instead.</desc>
      <rect x="24" y="24" width="145" height="68" rx="4" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#444"/>
      <text x="96" y="52" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16">Engine</text><text x="96" y="73" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">T5 / T6 gasoline</text>
      <rect x="215" y="24" width="165" height="68" rx="4" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#444"/>
      <text x="297" y="52" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16">Transmission</text><text x="297" y="73" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">Code to verify</text>
      <rect x="430" y="24" width="140" height="68" rx="4" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#444"/>
      <text x="500" y="52" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16">Front axle</text><text x="500" y="73" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">Front wheels</text>
      <rect x="215" y="222" width="165" height="68" rx="4" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#444"/>
      <text x="297" y="250" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16">Power take-off</text><text x="297" y="271" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">VIN-specific unit</text>
      <rect x="430" y="222" width="140" height="68" rx="4" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#444"/>
      <text x="500" y="250" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16">Propeller shaft</text><text x="500" y="271" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">Rearward drive</text>
      <rect x="620" y="222" width="116" height="68" rx="4" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#444"/>
      <text x="678" y="250" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15">Rear drive</text><text x="678" y="271" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">Rear axle</text>
      <path d="M169 58 H215 M380 58 H430" stroke="#333" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/>
      <path d="M297 92 V222 M380 256 H430 M570 256 H620" stroke="#333" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/>
      <path d="M405 51 l12 7 -12 7 M405 249 l12 7 -12 7 M595 249 l12 7 -12 7" fill="none" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="397" y="160" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#555">Power flow</text>
      <text x="380" y="325" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#555">Conceptual only — not to scale</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Conceptual AWD power-flow illustration. Component arrangement and service details are simplified.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>How the 2021 variants differ</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>T5 FWD:</strong> front-wheel drive; no rear propeller shaft or rear drive unit.</li>
    <li><strong>T5 AWD and T6 AWD:</strong> mechanical AWD layout represented by the diagram.</li>
    <li><strong>T8 Recharge:</strong> plug-in hybrid; the gasoline engine drives the front axle and an electric motor drives the rear axle. This is not the same parts layout as mechanical AWD.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note"><strong>Important:</strong> Do not use the mechanical AWD diagram to identify T8 components, and do not order AWD parts from the badge alone. Confirm the powertrain and VIN-specific component application.</p>

  <h2>What this diagram does not establish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Exact transmission model, gear ratios, or fluid specification.</li>
    <li>Exact angle-gear, coupling, or rear-drive-unit part numbers.</li>
    <li>Fluid capacities, service intervals, or torque values.</li>
    <li>Control-module wiring or diagnostic test points.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Volvo references</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.volvocars.com/is/support/car/s60-recharge-plug-in-hybrid/20w46/article/b0804d54c7fc096bc0a81f6f065ad63e/8899be1dc7fc78b1c0a81f6f5a01b4ab/00d308891f0cc443c0a80151619a46e9/">Volvo — 2021 S60 Recharge engine specifications</a>. Volvo identifies the electric rear axle drive (ERAD) as the rear electric drive motor; the page also notes market-specific engine availability.</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.volvotechinfo.com/">Volvo Technical Information</a> — VIN-specific service and diagnostic procedures.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For any repair, use the VIN-specific service procedure and confirm the component physically fitted to the vehicle.</p>
</BaseLayout>
